{
  "_comment": [
    "Hand-written player save for Biscuit, the level-36 player in level.mini.json.",
    "",
    "Not a redaction of a real file, unlike level.mini.json: a real player save is",
    "66-111 KB of RecordData maps that say nothing this needs to say. This is the",
    "smallest tree readPlayerSave will accept, and every id in it is one that",
    "level.mini.json actually contains, which is the whole point — it exists so the",
    "incremental flows can be driven rather than only reasoned about:",
    "",
    "  - dropping this onto the loaded level merges it (0 of 2 player saves -> 1 of 2)",
    "  - dropping it *before* the level exercises the pendingPlayerFiles hold",
    "  - editing PlayerUId to any other GUID exercises the foreign-uid refusal",
    "",
    "PlayerUId and InstanceId are Biscuit's, from the level's",
    "CharacterSaveParameterMap. CommonContainerId is the one item container in the",
    "level that nothing else claims, so attributing it here moves a container from",
    "unattributed to exact instead of colliding with a structure and raising an",
    "ownership-conflict warning. PalStorageContainerId holds the two pals whose",
    "OwnerPlayerUId is Biscuit's, so the majority vote and the player save agree.",
    "",
    "Timestamp is the level's own Timestamp to the tick, as a real pair has — both",
    "are written by the same save operation. LastOnlineDateTime is earlier, so",
    "last-seen resolves on the absolute clock instead of reading `online at save`.",
    "",
    "Keys the reader does not touch are omitted rather than stubbed. Anything in",
    "RecordData outside KNOWN_RECORD_FIELDS raises a counted warning, so the fields",
    "below are deliberately a subset of that set."
  ],
